    "Corpus validation rejects completed throughput bundles when len(stream_results) differs from integer run.streams, or config.streams when run.streams is absent; absent configured counts skip the check. The error names the bundle path and both counts. Failed and partial phases with truncated results do not hard-fail corpus validation solely for the count mismatch.",
    "Explorer excludes every completed throughput stream-count mismatch from ranking regardless of benchmark family or primary metric, including geomean-ranked SSB/ClickBench. Use stream_count_mismatch when no higher-priority exclusion already applies. Local result import withholds Throughput@Size for a completed mismatch.",
    "Failed and partial phases preserve phase-status exclusion behavior and are not relabeled as stream_count_mismatch.",
    "Tests cover matching counts, absent configured counts, run.streams/config.streams mismatches, failed/partial truncation, and completed SSB/ClickBench mismatches whose geomean metric must remain unranked."
